# ReMedFiLM V8 — Result Reconciliation

**Question.** Three macro-Dice values circulate for VAL808: approximately `0.837290` (ReMedFiLM FULL), `0.837862` (also labelled ReMedFiLM FULL in V5–V7), and `0.835080`. Which is the evaluation of the proposed four-component model, and what are the others?

**Verdict.** The proposed model's canonical VAL808 macro Dice is **`0.837290`**. `0.835080` is the **GlobalMedFiLM backbone** — the legitimate comparator, not a competing FULL value. `0.837862` is **not a measurement**: it is the arithmetic mean of three numbers hardcoded into the V5/V6/V7 report generators, and it is contradicted by the frozen three-seed archive it claims to cite. V8 rejects it. **This is a resolved reporting inconsistency, not a second experimental configuration.**

---

## 1. Canonical identity chain

| Field | Verified value |
|---|---|
| Proposed system | ReMedFiLM FULL = RA-MedFiLM-BARR = `G` + `R_psi` + `B_phi` + `S_omega` |
| Verified parameters | 4,837,420 |
| Population | VAL808 (held-out validation), n = 808 |
| Seed | 42 |
| Router threshold | `tau_C8 = -0.024358327623641256` |
| ROI / safety / output thresholds | 0.3 / 0.5 / 0.5 |
| Router decisions | SKIP 529 · EXECUTE 279 |
| Branches | EXECUTE_THEN_ACCEPT 266 · EXECUTE_THEN_REJECT 13 · SKIP_GLOBAL 529 |
| FULL macro Dice | **0.837289686002** |
| GlobalMedFiLM macro Dice | 0.835079717768 |
| Paired Δ | **+0.002209968233** (95% CI +0.001147693 to +0.003292050) |
| Aggregation | equal-weight mean of four per-domain per-image Dice means |

Independent cross-checks, all reproducible without any new inference:

* Re-scoring the 808 saved Phase 27 masks (`*_global.png`, `*_final.png`) gives `0.837289686`.
* The frozen per-sample three-seed archive gives seed-42 macro `0.837289105` (difference `5.81e-07`).
* The same archive gives backbone macro `0.835078960` (difference `7.58e-07`).
* All 808 cases are accounted for; for all 529 SKIP cases the saved FULL mask is byte-identical to the backbone mask.

## 2. `0.835079` is the comparator, not a discrepancy

`0.835080` is the frozen Phase 21 `GlobalMedFiLM` backbone evaluated on the same 808 images. GlobalMedFiLM is the first component of the proposed system and a legitimate ablation baseline. It is **not** the complete proposed model and must never be labelled ReMedFiLM FULL. The scientific result of the assembly is the *paired* difference `+0.002210` (`+0.2210` percentage points), not either absolute number in isolation.

## 3. Where `0.837862` actually comes from

V5, V6 and V7 report the same three-seed reproducibility triplet and then print its mean as the headline seed-42 result:

| Quantity | V5/V6/V7 printed value |
|---|---|
| seed 42 macro Dice | 0.837862 |
| seed 123 macro Dice | 0.837910 |
| seed 3407 macro Dice | 0.837815 |
| mean | 0.837862 |
| SD | 0.00004750 |

The arithmetic mean of those three values is `0.837862333` — i.e. the value printed as **both** the seed-42 row and the three-seed mean is the *mean*. That is internally inconsistent: the seed-42 cell was overwritten with the mean. `build_v7_pdf_report.py` additionally prints routing counts 183 selected / 165 accepted / 31 rejected, which cannot be reconciled with the frozen state machine (279 / 266 / 13).

The V7 QA document claims the triplet was traced to the frozen archive `data_cache/phase29_phase_d_canonical/phase29_phase_d_three_seed_val808_delta_dice.npz`. That archive exists and was re-read for V8. Re-aggregating it with the same equal-domain-weight rule gives:

| Seed | Genuine macro Dice from frozen NPZ | V7 printed | Difference |
|---|---|---|---|
| 42 | 0.837289105 | 0.837862 | -0.000572895 |
| 123 | 0.838466901 | 0.837910 | +0.000556901 |
| 3407 | 0.837947761 | 0.837815 | +0.000132761 |
| **mean** | **0.837901256** | 0.837862 | +0.000038922 |
| SD (ddof=1) | 0.000590273 | 0.000047501 | — |

None of the three V7 numbers appears in the archive. The genuine across-seed SD is `0.000590273`, roughly **12× larger** than V7's `0.000047501`: V7 understated seed-to-seed variability by more than an order of magnitude. This matters because all three seeds share one pre-trained backbone, so the triplet is descriptive component-initialisation stability, **not** three independent end-to-end training replicates.

A separate frozen record, `reports/audits/phase29_val808_seedwise_metrics.json`, gives a second genuine descriptive triplet (0.837351, 0.838511, 0.838000; mean 0.837954, SD 0.000581270). Its seed-42 entry reports `0.8373512` with 268 accepted cases rather than the 266 encoded in the saved masks. Those two extra safety decisions were never persisted as separate refined outputs, so this variant is **genuinely recorded but not re-derivable**; it is disclosed, not selected.

## 4. Policy sweep

`full_doc_report/REMEDFILM_FULL_RESULT_RECONCILIATION.json` tested every routing policy expressible from the saved masks (8 policies), including top-181/183/185/200/250/279 by utility and the threshold rule without the safety gate. Verdict recorded there: `REPORTING_INCONSISTENCY`; `any_policy_reproduces_0837862 = False`. No policy reproduces `0.837862`.

## 5. Additional V8-discovered conflicts (excluded from V8 tables)

| Legacy artifact | Conflict | V8 action |
|---|---|---|
| `tables/REMEDFILM_MODEL_COMPARISON.csv` | The four `dice_*` cells of the ReMedFiLM FULL row are **single-sample** Dice values, not domain means (each matches exactly one row of the per-sample table). The row's macro value is correct but its per-domain values are not. | Excluded; baselines taken from `reports/tables/phase21_six_model_comparison.csv`, FULL from the canonical re-score. |
| `PROGRESSION_AND_PROPAGATION_EVIDENCE.csv` | Stage 4 records `0.837862` with routed 0.2265, accepted 0.2042, +0.2783 pp and harm 0.1878; the frozen state machine gives routed 0.3453, accepted 0.3292, +0.2210 pp and harm 0.1200. | Excluded; superseded by `REMEDFILM_ABLATION_AND_PROGRESSION.csv`. |
| `tables/ReMedFiLM_External_Routing_Safety_V7.csv` | External routing counts (e.g. CVC 118 / 35 / 83) conflict with the frozen `c1_external_stress_*` artifacts. | Excluded; V8 uses the frozen external tables. |
| `tables/subgroup_performance_summary.csv` | V3-era table with macro 0.8379 / +0.28 pp. | Excluded. |

## 6. What V8 reports

| Context | Value | Status |
|---|---|---|
| Headline VAL808 ReMedFiLM FULL macro Dice, seed 42 | **0.837290** | canonical, reproducible |
| GlobalMedFiLM backbone on the same split | 0.835080 | comparator |
| Net paired gain | **+0.2210 pp** | 95% CI excludes zero |
| Three-seed descriptive mean (frozen NPZ) | 0.837901 ± 0.000590 | descriptive only; shared backbone |
| Phase 29 seedwise recorded mean | 0.837954 ± 0.000581 | recorded variant, not re-derivable |
| `0.837862` and +0.28 pp | — | **superseded; not used anywhere in V8** |

## 7. Consequence for the accuracy–cost figure

V7 paired `0.837862` with 34.72 GMACs (the always-refine cost), so its ReMedFiLM point was wrong on both axes. V8 plots the FULL system as its own marker at `0.837290` and **32.437902022582854** expected conditional GMACs. Because the baseline protocols are historical descriptive comparisons rather than matched controlled experiments, the chart is captioned as a **historical descriptive comparison**, not a confirmed Pareto frontier.

## 8. Unresolved (not silently repaired)

* The two-case difference between the Phase 29 seedwise record (268 accepted) and the saved-mask state (266 accepted) cannot be reconstructed from persisted artifacts.
* `0.837862` has no artifact, no policy and no consistent sample accounting behind it; it is rejected rather than re-labelled as a legitimate alternative configuration.
* C1 (learned vs identity FiLM), C2 (causal safety-gate attribution; A8 vs A7 CI includes zero), and C3 (matched multi-seed baseline matrix) remain `NOT_ESTABLISHED`. No controlled study is implied here.

